0017-gpui-webview-record-decorations.patch (combined series, 2026-11-13). Formerly 0017-gpui-webview-record-decorations.patch (original kept in nsh-host-patches/superseded-2026-11-13/).
Applies with patch -p1 at the root of a copy of nsh-host-allspeech-src after every earlier patch of the series 0010-0020, in order.

gpui: webview.recordInput (recording cursor decorations drawn onto recorded frames)

On top of 0016 (webview.recordStart / webview.recordStop). recordStart gains an optional decorations
{ showKeyPresses, showMousePresses, primaryColor: {r,g,b,a} 0..1 } (ignored by a host without this patch).
webview.recordInput takes the reference's DesktopPreviewRecordingInput ({type:"clear"} |
{type:"key",label,held,width} | {type:"pointer",phase,x,y,width,height}, DOM points) from the page's own
recording cursor and updates the active recording's decoration state; append() draws the click ring and the
key-label badge onto each appended frame with CoreGraphics (ring) and NSAttributedString/NSFont/NSColor
(the badge's text), the port of recordingCompositor.ts. Links AppKit (already linked); no new crate, no
Cargo.lock change.

